```

---

## 8️⃣ Performance & SEO

| Technique | How |
|-----------|-----|
| **Code Splitting** | Automatic with Next.js dynamic imports |
| **Image Optimization** | `next/image` with `layout="responsive"` |
| **Lazy Loading** | `loading="lazy"` on images, `React.lazy` for heavy components |
| **SSR / SSG** | Use `getStaticProps` for product pages, `getServerSideProps` for cart |
| **Meta Tags** | `next/head` for title, description, Open Graph |
| **Structured Data** | JSON‑LD for products, breadcrumbs |

---

## 9️⃣ Accessibility Checklist

| Check | Implementation |
|-------|----------------|
| **Keyboard Navigation** | Ensure all interactive elements are focusable |
| **ARIA Labels** | `aria-label="Add to cart"` on buttons |
| **Contrast Ratio** | Verify WCAG 2.1 AA using tools like axe |
| **Skip Links** | `<a href="#main">Skip to content</a>` |
| **Alt Text** | All images have descriptive `alt` attributes |

---

## 🔟 Testing Strategy

| Test Type | Tool | Focus |
|-----------|------|-------|
| **Unit** | Jest + React Testing Library | Component rendering, props |
| **Integration** | Cypress | End‑to‑end flows (login → checkout) |
| **Visual Regression** | Percy | UI consistency across releases |
| **Accessibility** | axe-core | Automated ARIA checks |

Example unit test:

```tsx
// src/components/__tests__/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render } from '@testing-library/react';
import ProductCard from '../ProductCard';

test('renders product title', () => {
  const product = { id: '1', title: 'Test', slug: 'test', image: '/img.png', price: 19.99 };
  const { getByText } = render(<ProductCard product={product} />);
  expect(getByText('Test')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

---

## 1️⃣1️⃣ Deployment & CI/CD

| Platform | Pros | Typical Workflow |
|----------|------|------------------|
| **Vercel** | Zero‑config, instant preview | GitHub → Vercel → Deploy |
| **Netlify** | Edge functions, split testing | GitHub → Netlify → Deploy |
| **AWS Amplify** | Full‑stack, CI/CD pipelines | GitHub → Amplify → Deploy |
| **Docker** | Custom infra | Dockerfile → ECS/EKS → Deploy |

**CI Pipeline (GitHub Actions)**

```yaml
name: CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
  pull_request:

jobs:
  build-test:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
        with:
          node-version: '20'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm run test
      - run: npm run build
```

---

## 1️⃣2️⃣ Monitoring & Analytics

| Tool | Use Case |
|------|----------|
| **Sentry** | Runtime error tracking |
| **LogRocket** | Session replay, performance |
| **Google Analytics / Plausible** | User behavior |
| **New Relic** | Backend performance (if you host APIs) |

